# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env for local development.
# .env is gitignored — never commit real credentials.
#
# Square credentials and payment mode are managed in the Keystatic admin UI.
# The only things that live here are secrets that the Worker needs at runtime.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── Keystatic CMS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed locally if you want to run Keystatic in GitHub mode.
# Leave blank for local dev (it auto-switches to local file mode).
KEYSTATIC_SECRET=

# ─── Square Access Tokens (Cloudflare Worker secrets — set once, never change) ─
# These are never stored in this file in production.
# Set them with:
#   npx wrangler secret put SQUARE_ACCESS_TOKEN_SANDBOX
#   npx wrangler secret put SQUARE_ACCESS_TOKEN_PRODUCTION
#
# Get them from developer.squareup.com → your app → Sandbox/Production tab → Access Token
# Sandbox token starts with:    EAAAlxxxxxxx  (from Sandbox tab)
# Production token starts with: EAAAlxxxxxxx  (from Production tab, looks the same but different value)

# ─── Resend (confirmation emails — Cloudflare Worker secrets) ─────────────────
# Set them with:
#   npx wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY
#   npx wrangler secret put RESEND_FROM_EMAIL
#
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL must match a verified domain or email in your Resend account.
